{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1728","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1728","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1728\",\"parent_revision\":\"daf096bccc91ee527a17df6f93061a4ebe741d3f\",\"root_revision\":\"fb4b797b499c936b9a1d4d18708b986efc1ac7ad5a62dcca03e60b9d3b9b7d04\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400` in server.py | AVAILABLE | Item description |\\n| 2 | `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` value | AVAILABLE | Item description cites server.py:1827-1828 |\\n| 3 | All four tool descriptions in server.py | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 documentation-only change, all values known.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer reading the documentation**, I want to **backlog mcp tool descriptions do not document the 10k-token-per-call ceiling** so that **documentation is accurate and trustworthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Cross-cutting concern from chunked-I/O research 2026-04-12\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Docs. Trivial change. No functional impact. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `backlog_list` description updated to: state the auto-pagination 4400-token budget explicitly; explain offset/limit vs page/tokens_per_page precedence; explain when to use each axis\\n- `backlog_view` description updated to: state its separate token budget (value TBD from `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`); explain progressive disclosure pattern (summary=True then targeted sections)\\n- `artifact_read` description updated to: state what happens when artifact exceeds ceiling (truncation/rejection); recommend chunked reading if artifact may be large\\n- `artifact_get` description updated to: explicitly say 'use this when you only need to check metadata, not read content'\\n- No functional code changes \u2014 description strings only\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 update tool description strings for backlog_list, backlog_view, artifact_read, artifact_get\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an LLM calling backlog_core MCP tools, I need the tool descriptions to document the per-call token ceiling and canonical pagination patterns so I can construct calls that stay under the limit without trial-and-error.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-ux-analysis-verified.md` \u00a7c1, \u00a7c2\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification.md` \u00a7u3, \u00a7u4, \u00a7u6\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-chunked-io-verification-round2.md` \u00a7Q1, \u00a7Q3\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- LLMs retry failed large responses instead of paginating, wasting calls and producing inconsistent partial data.\\n- Agents default to `backlog_view(summary=False)` when a section filter would have been enough.\\n- New tool consumers have no documented mental model for \\\"how do I read a big thing in pieces\\\".\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nMCP tool responses are bounded by an external per-call ceiling (~10,000 tokens). That ceiling is not visible to the LLM constructing a tool call \u2014 it is not in the tool descriptions registered by `backlog_core/server.py`, and it is not in the parameter `Field(description=...)` strings.\\n\\nWhen a response exceeds the ceiling, the tool framework truncates or rejects the call. The LLM has no prior signal that (a) a ceiling exists, (b) which parameters let it stay under it, or (c) what the canonical pagination pattern is.\\n\\nSpecific gaps, verified in session:\\n\\n- `backlog_list` has three overlapping pagination axes (`offset/limit`, `page/tokens_per_page/page_token_limit`) and a global `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET = 4_400`. The docstring mentions \\\"auto-pagination keeps the response under 4400 tokens\\\" but does not explain precedence.\\n- `backlog_view` uses a separate `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` (server.py:1827-1828) with different semantics, not cross-referenced.\\n- `artifact_read` has no pagination and no description of what happens when the artifact exceeds the ceiling.\\n- `artifact_get` returns metadata only, but the description does not say \\\"use this when you only need to check state, not read the content\\\" \u2014 which is the usage that keeps callers under the ceiling.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5fa3df4585a8f35c1e2247a084da250662cc6c81f57194630dedd64711f7731c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPt0plA\"}"}